WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:02.090
- No, you have an anniversary
coming up though, right?

00:00:02.090 --> 00:00:02.923
Is it three years?

00:00:02.923 --> 00:00:03.756
- Yeah, three year--

00:00:03.756 --> 00:00:04.589
- [Kelly] Yeah, with your wife?

00:00:04.589 --> 00:00:05.487
- Yeah, that's right,
I have a three year--

00:00:05.487 --> 00:00:06.320
- [Kelly] Yes, congratulations!

00:00:06.320 --> 00:00:07.153
- Thank you!

00:00:07.153 --> 00:00:07.986
Thank you very much.

00:00:07.986 --> 00:00:08.819
(audience cheers)

00:00:08.819 --> 00:00:11.360
- I'm married, I love being
married, I love my husband,

00:00:11.360 --> 00:00:13.781
but it is interesting to
bring two worlds together.

00:00:13.781 --> 00:00:16.014
(audience cheers)

00:00:16.014 --> 00:00:18.710
And especially, this is
why I brought it up too.

00:00:18.710 --> 00:00:21.050
'Cause my husband and I work,
'cause we're in the industry,

00:00:21.050 --> 00:00:23.410
but we're of different
cloths in the industry.

00:00:23.410 --> 00:00:25.315
He's in management and I'm
an artist, so it's different,

00:00:25.315 --> 00:00:28.300
so, two artists, enjoy. (laughs)

00:00:28.300 --> 00:00:29.834
- Yeah, no, for sure, I mean,

00:00:29.834 --> 00:00:31.808
we're cut from two
different cloths as well,

00:00:31.808 --> 00:00:36.690
she's brilliant and...

00:00:38.187 --> 00:00:39.020
I am her husband.

00:00:39.020 --> 00:00:39.853
- [Kelly] And you...

00:00:39.853 --> 00:00:40.686
(laughter)

00:00:40.686 --> 00:00:42.508
And, I sometimes
misconstrue 'and' and 'but'

00:00:42.508 --> 00:00:43.928
- [Thomas] Yeah. (laughs)

00:00:43.928 --> 00:00:46.870
And I'm the guy who screws
up Aaron Sorkin dialogue.

00:00:46.870 --> 00:00:48.778
No, we do, we have our
anniversary coming up

00:00:48.778 --> 00:00:50.940
and it's a tricky thing,

00:00:50.940 --> 00:00:53.620
negotiating relationships
inside the industry

00:00:53.620 --> 00:00:54.453
and all that sort of stuff, but--

00:00:54.453 --> 00:00:55.286
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:00:55.286 --> 00:00:56.840
- But, it's mostly just has to do with

00:00:56.840 --> 00:00:59.330
parenting and whose gonna be
around and what you're gonna do

00:00:59.330 --> 00:01:03.200
and how close do you want your
kids to be to this industry

00:01:03.200 --> 00:01:04.033
and all that sort of stuff.

00:01:04.033 --> 00:01:06.449
- That is a constant
battle within myself...

00:01:06.449 --> 00:01:07.282
- [Mark] Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:01:07.282 --> 00:01:08.237
- Because you want them to be
a part of what you're doing,

00:01:08.237 --> 00:01:09.470
you want them around,
but then you're like,

00:01:09.470 --> 00:01:11.490
this isn't normal and you're
kinda being weird about it.

00:01:11.490 --> 00:01:13.945
- We both are, like, super
working class kids, like, we...

00:01:13.945 --> 00:01:14.778
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:01:14.778 --> 00:01:17.320
- You know what I mean? I grew
up in a small town in Texas

00:01:17.320 --> 00:01:18.630
and she grew up in Pennsylvania,

00:01:18.630 --> 00:01:21.197
and, we don't want this.

00:01:21.197 --> 00:01:22.030
- Yeah, yeah.

00:01:22.030 --> 00:01:24.250
- Like, we never, it's what
we do, it's not who we are.

00:01:24.250 --> 00:01:25.083
- Yeah.

00:01:25.083 --> 00:01:26.808
- And that's not exactly
what we wanna take to.

00:01:26.808 --> 00:01:28.015
(audience claps)

00:01:28.015 --> 00:01:29.797
- Yeah, but, at the same time,

00:01:29.797 --> 00:01:32.522
coming from a small
town Texas girl as well,

00:01:32.522 --> 00:01:33.355
- [Thomas] Sure.

00:01:33.355 --> 00:01:34.188
- It's nice that, though,
that they are in it

00:01:34.188 --> 00:01:35.580
and it's not all the (gasp)

00:01:35.580 --> 00:01:36.920
'cause they're 'round
it all the time, so...

00:01:36.920 --> 00:01:38.660
- Oh, she, she's gonna be so bored of it.

00:01:38.660 --> 00:01:39.960
- [Kelly] Yeah, she's three, right?

00:01:39.960 --> 00:01:40.793
- She is, she is.

00:01:40.793 --> 00:01:42.170
- [Kelly] Oh, 'cause I have
a three year old, as well.

00:01:42.170 --> 00:01:43.480
One of ours is three.

00:01:43.480 --> 00:01:44.680
I call it a threenager.

00:01:44.680 --> 00:01:45.513
- [Thomas] Yes.

00:01:45.513 --> 00:01:46.346
- Yeah.

00:01:46.346 --> 00:01:47.179
- [Thomas] Yes.

00:01:47.179 --> 00:01:48.012
- [Kelly] Full on fit.

00:01:48.012 --> 00:01:49.640
- She has quite a lot of opinions,

00:01:49.640 --> 00:01:51.900
she is not afraid of expressing them,

00:01:51.900 --> 00:01:54.580
- That's kind of a bold girl, I like it.

00:01:54.580 --> 00:01:56.690
- She's tough, she's tough as nails.

00:01:56.690 --> 00:01:58.010
- [Kelly] You want her to be like that.

00:01:58.010 --> 00:02:01.562
- Oh, I do, I totally do, and
she's gonna grind me down.

00:02:01.562 --> 00:02:03.467
(laughter)

00:02:03.467 --> 00:02:05.557
I look at it already and I'm like,

00:02:05.557 --> 00:02:06.950
"I am a broken man already."

00:02:06.950 --> 00:02:09.700
- Yeah, no, literally,
mine do the same thing,

00:02:09.700 --> 00:02:10.533
I'll look at my husband like,

00:02:10.533 --> 00:02:13.022
"Why are they so mean
sometimes? I'm like--"

00:02:13.022 --> 00:02:15.270
- Like, I just wanna make you happy.

00:02:15.270 --> 00:02:17.240
- [Kelly] I know, and I,
and I always do that thing

00:02:17.240 --> 00:02:18.620
where they're like, "Why do
you always have to go to work?"

00:02:18.620 --> 00:02:20.777
and I'm like, "Do you like your house?"

00:02:20.777 --> 00:02:22.330
"Do you like your Barbies?"

00:02:22.330 --> 00:02:23.163
I'm like--

00:02:23.163 --> 00:02:23.996
- You know what, it's like, yeah,

00:02:23.996 --> 00:02:25.250
but not as much as I like my mom.

00:02:25.250 --> 00:02:26.083
- [Kelly] No, but that's not fair...

00:02:26.083 --> 00:02:27.690
- And then you go (cries)

00:02:27.690 --> 00:02:30.440
- That's not fair though,
because my mom was a single mom

00:02:30.440 --> 00:02:33.310
and wasn't able to be
around a lot, and I'm great!

00:02:33.310 --> 00:02:34.788
I turned out fine!

00:02:34.788 --> 00:02:36.556
- Undeniably, undeniably.

00:02:36.556 --> 00:02:38.280
- So, I always tell her, I'm like...

00:02:38.280 --> 00:02:39.139
- [Thomas] Oh, no, no don't...

00:02:39.139 --> 00:02:40.090
- [Kelly] Don't you pull that crap on me!

00:02:40.090 --> 00:02:41.980
- Don't get me wrong,
I mean, it's definitely

00:02:41.980 --> 00:02:43.120
one of those things
where you gotta put them

00:02:43.120 --> 00:02:45.430
in their place about that
stuff, you know what I mean?

00:02:45.430 --> 00:02:46.366
But it--

00:02:46.366 --> 00:02:47.199
- Yes, I don't care what Mia's mom

00:02:47.199 --> 00:02:50.366
gets to do with you,
that's awesome, I can't.

00:02:50.366 --> 00:02:52.740
- [Mark] Yes, that's right.

00:02:52.740 --> 00:02:54.203
- [Kelly] I do other things.

